title: 'Westend system chains: derive KickThreshold from the largest collator set'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `parachains-common` adds `impls::KickThreshold`, a `Get` for the `KickThreshold` of
    `pallet-collator-selection` on a chain whose Aura set holds up to `ExtraCollators` more
    collators than collator selection's invulnerables and candidates, for example validators
    drawn by `pallet-validator-collators`. It returns two rounds of the largest collator set plus
    two slots, then the first whole number of sessions above that, since candidates are only
    kicked at session start. Aura picks the author as the slot modulo the set length, so a change
    of the set length at a session boundary can delay a collator's next turn by up to one more
    round. A candidate authors a block within that time, across one such change, and is not
    kicked as stale. The runtime supplies the extra collators, the
    blocks it authors per Aura slot and its session length.

    Asset Hub Westend and People Westend configure their `KickThreshold` with this helper, using
    `MaxValidators` of `pallet-validator-collators` as the extra collators, and expose the blocks
    they author per Aura slot as the public `BlocksPerAuraSlot` parameter type.
crates:
- name: parachains-common
  bump: minor
- name: pallet-validator-collators
  bump: none
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: minor
- name: people-westend-runtime
  bump: minor
